<title>NIGERIA: Budget delay still dampens Nigerian forex demand.</title>
<headline>Budget delay still dampens Nigerian forex demand.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's central bank said on Friday it sold $887,494 at a rate of 80 naira to the dollar, far below last year's weekly average.</p>
<p>Last week the bank sold $76,224 at the same rate. The average sale at last year's weekly auctions was $20 million.</p>
<p>Bankers said demand remained low in anticipation of the 1997 budget which the military government has been due to announce since January 1.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to be cautious when there may be changes to foreign exchange policy which could affect the rate,&quot; said one banker.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
